ASSESSMENT

Primary Diagnosis: Acute Autonomic Crisis / Somatic Pain Flare secondary to Sequelae of Intimate Partner Violence - PTSD - V61.11 - Status: Exacerbated
Differentials:

Acute Occult Trauma (e.g., Rib Fracture/Internal Injury) - Ruled out/unlikely based on the patient's explicit denial of recent acute physical assault, the absence of localized bruising or peritonism, and the diffuse, symmetrical nature of the somatic pain.

Acute Coronary Syndrome - Ruled out/unlikely due to the reproducible chest wall tenderness, normal oxygen saturation, and symptoms directly correlating with the acute psychological trauma of the relationship conflict.

Fibromyalgia (Primary) - Ruled out/unlikely as the primary, isolated diagnosis; while a central sensitization pain syndrome is present, it is entirely secondary to and driven by the active, severe trauma of ongoing intimate partner violence.
